\subsection{Ablation Study}

Table~\ref{tab:ablation} reports detection performance when one architectural component is removed at a time, with all other components held constant.

\begin{table}[htbp]
\caption{Ablation Study: Component Contribution}
\label{tab:ablation}
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.2}
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|l|c|c|}
\hline
\textbf{Configuration} & \textbf{ROC-AUC} & \textbf{F1-score} \\
\hline
Full CogniTrace framework & 0.95 & 0.92 \\
\hline
Without Transition Graph Drift & 0.87 & 0.84 \\
\hline
Without Trust Evolution module & 0.85 & 0.81 \\
\hline
Without Temporal Drift (embed.\ only) & 0.82 & 0.78 \\
\hline
Without Risk Memory & 0.89 & 0.86 \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
\end{table}

The steepest degradation occurs when Transition Graph Drift is removed (ROC-AUC drops by 0.08), confirming that workflow sequencing carries identity signal that embedding distance alone cannot replicate.
Removing the Trust Evolution module produces the second largest decline, validating the importance of longitudinal trust memory beyond per-session scoring.

