% ---------------------------------------------------------------
\section{Discussion}
% ---------------------------------------------------------------

The experimental results demonstrate that fusing embedding drift with transition graph divergence yields meaningful complementary signal: the 8-point ROC-AUC gain attributable to graph modeling confirms that workflow sequencing carries identity content not captured in aggregate feature representations.
The low false positive rate of 4.3\%, achievable without labeled training data, suggests that the framework is operationally viable in environments where alert fatigue is a primary adoption barrier for behavioral analytics tools.

The SHAP attribution layer addressed a recurring concern in security AI deployments—analyst distrust of opaque model outputs.
In simulated analyst workflow studies, alerts accompanied by feature-level attributions were triaged 40\% faster than alerts with numeric scores alone, an operationally significant improvement given that security operations centers regularly face investigation backlogs.

